trusted mint, then feed it to a second daemon configured for a different mint and
assert it is not credited (receive fails, balance stays 0). This is the
observable safety invariant behind the untrusted-mint guard.

Verified on GL-MT6000: 9 passed, 2 skipped (remaining: the two gonuts fork
funds-safety fixes, which need fault-injection infrastructure).
